# -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Core Files to IGNORE for Node.js/Express Project
# -----------------------------------------------------------------

# 1. Dependencies (Crucial: Keeps repository size small)
/node_modules

# 2. Environment Variables (Crucial: Security/Credentials)
# This prevents uploading your DB_USER, DB_PASS, etc., from your .env file
.env
.env.*
!.env.example  # Keep the .env.example file so others know what variables are needed

# 3. Logs and Temporary Files
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# 4. Built/Compiled Artifacts (If you were using a build tool, but good practice)
/dist
/build

# 5. Operating System / Editor Files
.DS_Store
.vscode